INT. SUPPLY CLOSET - FUN COMMITTEE HQ - DAY

A windowless closet with a laminated sign: FUN COMMITTEE. Shelves of streamers, foam trophies, and a half-inflated balloon arch. GERALDINE MWANGI, 40s, tightly wound, holds a clipboard. OSWALD PRUITT, 50s, soft-spoken facilities manager, holds a roll of tape.

GERALDINE
You were late to the committee.

OSWALD
I was fixing the ice machine.

GERALDINE
The committee is mandatory.

OSWALD
So is the ice machine.

GERALDINE
Is it? Is ice mandatory?

OSWALD
In July, ma'am, ice is the only thing that is.

GERALDINE
Don't "ma'am" me. I'm chair.

OSWALD
I know you're chair. You made the badge.

GERALDINE
It's a lanyard.

OSWALD
It's a lanyard that says CHAIR.

GERALDINE
Because I am the chair.

OSWALD
Of fun.

GERALDINE
Yes, Oswald. Of fun.

OSWALD
I just don't think fun has a chair.

GERALDINE
That is exactly what someone without fun would say.

OSWALD
Maybe so.

GERALDINE
Item one. The summer picnic.

OSWALD
Do we have a budget?

GERALDINE
We have four hundred dollars and a dream.

OSWALD
Four hundred dollars for two hundred people.

GERALDINE
Forty people.

OSWALD
Two hundred is on the slide.

GERALDINE
Forget the slide. Forty.

OSWALD
Ten dollars a head. That's a hot dog.

GERALDINE
That's a hot dog and joy.

OSWALD
Joy costs extra.

GERALDINE
Joy is free. Bun is extra.

OSWALD
Then we have a hot dog without a bun.

GERALDINE
Then it's a sausage with a dream.

OSWALD
I'd like that in writing.

GERALDINE
Item two. The dunk tank.

OSWALD
No.

GERALDINE
You haven't heard it.

OSWALD
I've heard enough. Dunk tanks are an insurance event.

GERALDINE
Legal says it's fine.

OSWALD
Legal is one man named Tyrone, and he said "probably."

GERALDINE
"Probably" is yes in a good tie.

OSWALD
Who volunteers to sit in the tank?

GERALDINE
The regional director.

OSWALD
Does the regional director know?

GERALDINE
He will when the invitation goes out.

OSWALD
So that's a no.

GERALDINE
That's a surprise yes.

OSWALD
I've worked here nineteen years. Nobody has ever been happy about a surprise.

GERALDINE
You've never run one properly.

OSWALD
I ran the fire drill.

GERALDINE
Nobody was happy about that either.

OSWALD
It was a fire drill, Geraldine.

GERALDINE
Item three. Morale.

OSWALD
Morale is not an item.

GERALDINE
Everything is an item.

OSWALD
Morale is weather. You can't put weather on a clipboard.

GERALDINE
I've put weather on a clipboard. It was Q3.

OSWALD
How did that go?

GERALDINE
It rained on the picnic.

OSWALD
Then what are we doing?

GERALDINE
We are making it better.

OSWALD
By what means?

GERALDINE
By streamers, Oswald. By trophies. By a balloon arch, which you will finish inflating.

OSWALD
I don't have a pump.

GERALDINE
You have lungs.

OSWALD
I have a bad one.

GERALDINE
Then you'll inflate it slowly and with feeling.

OSWALD
Is that in the bylaws?

GERALDINE
It's in the spirit of the bylaws.

OSWALD
Geraldine. Why did you take this on?

GERALDINE
Somebody had to.

OSWALD
Nobody had to.

GERALDINE
Somebody had to want to.

OSWALD
And that was you.

GERALDINE
That was me. Hold the clipboard.

OSWALD
I'm holding tape.

GERALDINE
Hold both.

OSWALD
Fine.

GERALDINE
Now. Item four.

OSWALD
How many items are there?

GERALDINE
Eleven.

OSWALD
It's four o'clock.

GERALDINE
Then we'd better start.
